Figure 11, presenting H&E stained muscle sections two weeks post-injection, demonstrates that Nano-11 adjuvant induces significantly less residual inflammation compared to aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. The left panel, representing AH, shows extensive granulomatous inflammation with dense inflammatory infiltrates and macrophage aggregates (inset). In contrast, the right panel, showing Nano-11, exhibits substantially milder inflammation characterized by relatively few macrophages arranged in slender cords within the connective tissue (inset). This visual evidence supports Nano-11's transient and less severe local inflammatory response, indicating a more favorable safety profile than AH.